# Declared again at the root, x is the same place (the book #shadowing-levels: a repeated declaration on the same
# level works with its existing place, and its RHS is assigned), so `int: seen x` gives 2. The root's sub main
# writes seen to `shared\Observed\seen`; it names the root by `node[0]`.
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
)
int: x 1
int: x 2
int: seen x
sub: main ()
    @: shared node[0]
    shared\Observed\seen := seen
main()
